EXAM_DATA.papers["2004"] = {"id":"2004","year":2004,"label":"2004 旧卷","era":"old","sourceUrl":"https://english-exam.lazynote.cn/kaoyan/paper/2004/","timeLimitMin":180,"scoreMode":"raw","parts":[{"id":"section1","kind":"cloze","title":"Section I 完形填空","directions":"Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET . (10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section1-1","text":"Many theories concerning the causes of juvenile delinquency (crimes committed by young people) focus either on the individual or on society as the major contributing influence. Theories   {{1}}   on the individual suggest that children engage in criminal behavior   {{2}}   they were not sufficiently penalized for previous misdeeds or that they have learned criminal behavior through   {{3}}   with others. Theories focusing on the role of society suggest that children commit crimes in   {{4}}   to their failure to rise above their socioeconomic status,   {{5}}   as a rejection of middle-class values."},{"id":"p-section1-2","text":"Most theories of juvenile delinquency have focused on children from disadvantaged families,   {{6}}   the fact that children from wealthy homes also commit crimes. The latter may commit crimes   {{7}}   lack of adequate parental control. All theories, however, are tentative and are   {{8}}   to criticism."},{"id":"p-section1-3","text":"Changes in the social structure may indirectly   {{9}}   juvenile crime rates. For example, changes in the economy that   {{10}}   to fewer job opportunities for youth and rising unemployment   {{11}}   make gainful employment increasingly difficult to obtain. The resulting discontent may in   {{12}}   lead more youths into criminal behavior."},{"id":"p-section1-4","text":"Families have also   {{13}}   changes these years. More families consist of one-parent households or two working parents;   {{14}}   , children are likely to have less supervision at home   {{15}}   was common in the traditional family   {{16}}   . This lack of parental supervision is thought to be an influence on juvenile crime rates. Other   {{17}}   causes of offensive acts include frustration or failure in school, the increased   {{18}}   of drugs and alcohol, and the growing   {{19}}   of child abuse and child neglect. All these conditions tend to increase the probability of a child committing a criminal act,   {{20}}   a direct causal relationship has not yet been established."}]},"questions":[{"n":1,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"acting"},{"key":"B","text":"relying"},{"key":"C","text":"centering"},{"key":"D","text":"commenting"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"1.","reason":"与下一句 \"focusing on the role of society\" 形成结构对照 线索就在同段下一句 Theories focusing on the role of society suggest that children commit crimes in __(4)__ to their failure…。两句结构完全平行：Theories ___ on X suggest that…，因此 ___ 必须与 focusing 同义，意为 \"聚焦于、以…为中心\"。这一同段平行线索把答案直接框死在 \"以…为焦点\" 这个语义上。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"acting 与 on 搭配多表示 \"对…采取行动\" 或 \"按照…行事\"，与平行句 focusing on the role of society 的 \"聚焦于\" 之意不对应。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"relying on 表 \"依赖于\"，意味着把个体当作工具或依据，与下一句 focusing on the role of society 的 \"以…为论述焦点\" 的并列含义不一致。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"center on 是 \"以…为中心、聚焦于…\" 的固定表达，直接对应下一句 Theories focusing on the role of society 中的 focusing on，使两类理论的并列论述结构成立。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"commenting on 是 \"评论…\"，仅指对某事发表看法，远不及 \"聚焦\" 的论述深度，且与下一句 focusing on 的对照不成立。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":2,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"before"},{"key":"B","text":"unless"},{"key":"C","text":"until"},{"key":"D","text":"because"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"2.","reason":"本句内 \"个人理论\" 的因果指向：惩罚不足 → 犯罪 线索就在空格前后：Theories __(1)__ on the individual suggest that children engage in criminal behavior __(2)__ they were not sufficiently penalized for previous misdeeds——这是 \"以个体为焦点的理论\" 对儿童犯罪原因的解释，\"以往恶行未受充分惩罚\" 显然是 \"产生犯罪行为\" 的原因。线索完全位于本句之内。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"before 仅表 \"在…之前\"，与 \"惩罚不足导致犯罪\" 这一理论解释完全不沾边。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"unless 意为 \"除非\"，代入后变成 \"除非他们没被充分惩罚，否则就犯罪\"，逻辑荒谬，与该理论 \"惩罚不足导致犯罪\" 完全相反。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"until 表 \"直到…\"，引出时间持续，无法解释为何 \"惩罚不足\" 是 \"犯罪\" 的成因。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"because 直接给出原因 \"因为以往恶行未被充分惩罚\"，正是 \"以个体为焦点的理论\" 解释儿童犯罪的因果机制；且与同句后半句 or that they have learned criminal behavior through __(3)__ with others 并列出该理论给出的两条原因，结构对称。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":3,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"interaction"},{"key":"B","text":"assimilation"},{"key":"C","text":"cooperation"},{"key":"D","text":"consultation"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"3.","reason":"本句已点明 \"通过…与他人 learn behavior\"，强调日常往来 线索在本句：they have learned criminal behavior through __(3)__ with others。\"通过与他人…习得犯罪行为\" 必须落在 \"日常社会交往\" 这种广义、双向的接触上；而上一空给出的 __(2)__ they were not sufficiently penalized 是与之并列的另一种成因，说明本句是经典的 \"模仿学习\" 视角——日常 interaction 是其前提。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"interaction 指人与人之间的相互作用，是社会学里 \"通过交往习得行为\" 的标准用词，与 with others 中性搭配天然契合，也呼应了 \"个体焦点理论\" 中习得论的标准表述。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"assimilation 强调一方被另一方吸收同化，指向单向过程，无法对应 \"通过与他人交往习得\" 这种双向互动的中性描述。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"cooperation 带正向 \"合作\" 色彩，且暗含共同目标，不能涵盖 \"看到别人这样做于是也学会\" 的一般性学习路径。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"consultation 仅指就专门事项征求意见，远不能覆盖儿童通过日常接触习得犯罪行为这一宽泛过程。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":4,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"return"},{"key":"B","text":"reply"},{"key":"C","text":"reference"},{"key":"D","text":"response"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"4.","reason":"上下文是 \"以社会为焦点\" 的理论给出 \"因→果\" 解释 线索见 Theories focusing on the role of society suggest that children commit crimes in __(4)__ to their failure to rise above their socioeconomic status——\"未能突破自身社会经济地位\" 是因，\"实施犯罪\" 是果；空格要表达的就是 \"对…的反应\"。in response to = \"作为对…的反应\" 是该语境标准说法。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"return 的常见搭配是 in return for（作为对…的回报），且 \"回报\" 与 \"因挫败而犯罪\" 的语境不符。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"reply 强调对言语类沟通的回答，对 \"挫败这一处境\" 用 reply 不合习惯，固定搭配也偏向 in reply to your letter 之类。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"reference 的固定搭配 in reference to 意为 \"关于、提及\"，仅表话题指向，无法表达 \"对挫败的反应\" 这种行为因果。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"response 与 in / to 构成 in response to，正是 \"作为对（挫败）的反应\" 这一标准说法，精确承载该理论 \"挫败 → 犯罪\" 的因果链。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":5,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"or"},{"key":"B","text":"but rather"},{"key":"C","text":"but"},{"key":"D","text":"or else"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"5.","reason":"前后是 \"社会焦点理论\" 给出的两种并列解释，可同时成立 线索见 children commit crimes in __(4)__ to their failure to rise above their socioeconomic status, __(5)__ as a rejection of middle-class values——\"对挫败的反应\" 与 \"对中产价值的拒斥\" 是该理论列举的两种平行解释，二者并不互斥，反而互补，因此空格应该是 \"或\" 这种并列选择关系，而非转折/否定。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"or 连接前后两种解释 \"对挫败的反应\" 与 \"对中产价值的拒斥\"，表示该理论既可这样解释也可那样解释，是社会焦点理论内的两种并列陈述，逻辑最顺。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"but rather 表 \"而非/而是\"，必须搭配前文一个 not 否定句才合习惯，且会把 \"对挫败的反应\" 否定掉，与本句两种解释并列共存的语义直接冲突。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"but 表转折，会让 \"对中产价值的拒斥\" 与 \"对挫败的反应\" 对立起来，但原文显示这是同一理论的两种并列解释，没有对立关系。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"or else 通常用于警告 \"否则会有…后果\"（do X, or else…），与本句陈述两种并列原因的语境完全不符。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":6,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"considering"},{"key":"B","text":"ignoring"},{"key":"C","text":"highlighting"},{"key":"D","text":"discarding"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"6.","reason":"主句聚焦弱势家庭，但事实是富裕家庭也犯罪，隐含转折 线索在本句：Most theories…have focused on children from disadvantaged families, __(6)__ the fact that children from wealthy homes also commit crimes.——前半句说大多数理论只盯着贫困家庭，后半句承认 \"富裕家庭孩子也犯罪\" 这一事实。两者构成 \"对事实的忽视\" 这种隐性批评：理论盯着 A，却 ___ 了事实 B。\"忽视/无视\" 是唯一与之逻辑自洽的动作。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"considering 表 \"考虑到\"，若选此意味着理论同时考虑了富裕家庭的事实，但主句明明说 \"have focused on…disadvantaged families\"，两者自相矛盾。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"ignoring 直白指出 \"忽视了富裕家庭孩子也犯罪这一事实\"，与主句 \"只盯着弱势家庭\" 形成自然的对照与批评，逻辑链顺畅。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"highlighting 是 \"突出强调\"，意味着理论刻意凸显了富裕家庭犯罪事实，与主句限定的关注面恰好相反。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"discarding 意为 \"抛弃、丢弃\"，多用于丢弃物品/想法，对 \"事实\" 而言通常用 ignore；且语气过强，与综述性中性表述不符。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":7,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"on"},{"key":"B","text":"in"},{"key":"C","text":"for"},{"key":"D","text":"with"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"7.","reason":"前是 \"犯罪行为\"，后是 \"管教缺失\"，关系是 \"出于…原因\" 线索见本句 The latter may commit crimes __(7)__ lack of adequate parental control.——commit crimes 是结果，lack of adequate parental control 是原因。表达 \"出于…原因/由于…\" 的常用介词是 for（do something for some reason）。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"on 在表 \"原因\" 时多见于 act on impulse，与 commit crimes on lack of… 搭配不成立。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"in 用在 in need of / in want of 这类固定短语，但 in lack of 并非英语固定搭配，且表达不出 \"出于…\" 的原因语义。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"for 表 \"由于、出于\"，commit crimes for lack of adequate parental control 即 \"由于管教不足而犯罪\"，是地道且语义精准的原因表达。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"with 多表伴随或凭借手段，与 \"由于管教不足\" 这一因果关系不对应。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":8,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"immune"},{"key":"B","text":"resistant"},{"key":"C","text":"sensitive"},{"key":"D","text":"subject"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"8.","reason":"前半句 tentative 已奠定 \"未定论、可被挑战\" 的基调 线索就在本句前半：All theories, however, are tentative and are __(8)__ to criticism.——并列连接词 and 要求空格语义与前半 tentative（暂定的、不确定的）同向。tentative 已表 \"待定、可被推翻\"，因此空格应是 \"易受批评/有待批评\" 的意思。be subject to criticism 正是 \"易遭批评\" 的固定说法。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"immune 表 \"免疫、不受影响\"，若代入则成为 \"理论免受批评\"，与前半 tentative \"还很初步\" 完全相反。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"resistant 表 \"抵抗、不易受影响\"，与 \"暂定、待考\" 的逻辑同样不一致。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"sensitive 表 \"对…敏感\"，常用于感官、情感或政治议题，把它用在 \"理论对批评敏感\" 上语义偏离，搭配也不地道。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"subject 与 to 构成 be subject to，意为 \"易受…、有待…\"，be subject to criticism 即 \"易遭批评、不能免于批评\"，与 tentative 同向，自然衔接。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":9,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"affect"},{"key":"B","text":"reduce"},{"key":"C","text":"chock"},{"key":"D","text":"reflect"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"9.","reason":"下一句给出具体路径，说明只是 \"影响\"，并非 \"减少\" 或 \"反映\" 线索见紧接的下一句 For example, changes in the economy that __(10)__ to fewer job opportunities for youth and rising unemployment __(11)__ make gainful employment increasingly difficult to obtain.——这是举例说明 \"社会结构变化如何通过经济渠道间接传导到青少年犯罪率\"。这种 \"通过中间链条传导\" 的关系，只能用中性词 affect（影响）来概括，不能是 reduce（减少，方向反了）或 reflect（反映，主客倒置）。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"affect 意为 \"影响\"，方向中性，可指向上升或下降，正好与 indirectly 搭配表达 \"间接地影响犯罪率\"，并由下句的经济传导例子展开。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"reduce 表 \"减少\"，但下一段例子讲的是经济变差→失业→不满→犯罪 \"增加\"，方向相反。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"chock 通常作名词或动词表 \"垫块、塞住\"，并非 \"影响/抑制犯罪率\" 的标准用语；即使取 choke 之义 \"抑制\"，也与下文 \"导致犯罪增加\" 的方向相悖。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"reflect 表 \"反映\"，应是 \"犯罪率反映社会结构变化\"，而非 \"社会结构变化反映犯罪率\"，主客错位。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":10,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"point"},{"key":"B","text":"lead"},{"key":"C","text":"come"},{"key":"D","text":"amount"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"10.","reason":"to 后是 \"工作机会减少 + 失业上升\"，明显为 \"结果\" 线索在本句：changes in the economy that __(10)__ to fewer job opportunities for youth and rising unemployment——\"工作机会减少和失业上升\" 是因果链中的 \"结果\"，因此 ___ to 必须是 \"导致\" 的意思。lead to 是表 \"导致\" 的最标准短语。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"point to 偏 \"指向、表明\"，主语通常是证据/事实，强调推论关系，而非 \"经济变化造成失业\" 这种实质性因果。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"lead 与 to 构成 lead to，正是 \"经济变化导致工作机会减少与失业上升\" 所需的因果连词，搭配地道、语义精准。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"come to 多表 \"达到、合计为\" 或 \"突然意识到\"，与 \"经济变化造成失业\" 这种动作型因果不匹配。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"amount to 用于数额总和或 \"等同于\"，宾语必须是数额或同类对象，不能搭配 \"工作机会减少\" 这种结果。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":11,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"in general"},{"key":"B","text":"on average"},{"key":"C","text":"by contrast"},{"key":"D","text":"at length"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"11.","reason":"上文给出经济传导链，本句作普遍性结论而非对比/数据 线索见上下文 For example, changes in the economy that __(10)__ to fewer job opportunities for youth and rising unemployment __(11)__ make gainful employment increasingly difficult to obtain.——前面已铺好 \"经济变化→工作机会少+失业升\" 的链条，本空所在的小句是对这一传导后果的普遍性总结 \"使获得稳定就业越来越难\"，并未对比另一组也未给出数据，因此应当是 in general（总体而言）。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"in general 表 \"大体上、总体而言\"，与本句对 \"经济变化→失业难就业\" 这一普遍后果作总结的语气完美匹配。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"on average 表 \"平均而言\"，需要有统计意义上的数据均值，本句并未涉及数字平均，语境不符。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"by contrast 必须有一个明确的对比对象出现在上文，但本句没有对比项，强行使用会让逻辑断裂。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"at length 表 \"详尽地\" 或 \"最终\"，要求随后是详尽展开或终于发生的动作，与本句简短总结的语气不合。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":12,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"case"},{"key":"B","text":"short"},{"key":"C","text":"turn"},{"key":"D","text":"essence"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"12.","reason":"上文给出 \"经济差→不满\"，本句续接 \"不满→犯罪\"，构成连锁反应 线索遍布第三段：changes in the economy that __(10)__ to fewer job opportunities for youth and rising unemployment __(11)__ make gainful employment increasingly difficult to obtain. The resulting discontent may in __(12)__ lead more youths into criminal behavior.——\"经济变化 → 失业 → 不满 → 犯罪\" 是一连串依次触发的因果链，本空表达的就是 \"反过来又…\"，正是 in turn（依次/转而）的语义。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"case 构成 in case 表 \"以防、万一\"，是条件性预防语义，与本句承接因果链的功能不符。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"short 构成 in short 用于对前文做整段总结，但本句仅承接一环 \"不满→犯罪\"，并非全段总结。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"turn 与 in 构成 in turn，意为 \"反过来又/依次\"，与上文 \"经济→失业→不满\" 接续 \"不满→犯罪\" 的链式因果完全合拍。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"essence 构成 in essence 强调 \"本质上是\"，用于揭示本质特征，与本句承接因果链的功能不符。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":13,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"survived"},{"key":"B","text":"noticed"},{"key":"C","text":"undertaken"},{"key":"D","text":"experienced"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"13.","reason":"下一句给出 \"单亲、双职工\" 这些社会变迁现象，是被动承受而非主动发起 线索见 More families consist of one-parent households or two working parents; __(14)__, children are likely to have less supervision at home __(15)__ was common in the traditional family __(16)__.——这些是社会层面的客观变化，对家庭而言是被动承受 \"经历\" 而非主动 \"承担\" 或 \"幸存\"。因此应填 experienced。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"survived 表 \"从…中幸存\"，多用于灾难/危机，搭配 changes 不合习惯，且语义过重。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"noticed 表 \"注意到\"，主语通常是人或观察者，家庭整体作为承载单位 notice changes 不合自然。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"undertaken 强调主动承担/开展，多用于机构主动推动；但本段后文 \"单亲、双职工\" 是社会变迁结果，并非家庭主动发起。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"experienced 意为 \"经历\"，与 \"家庭这些年经历了变化\" 完美对应：被动承受社会变迁，与下一句具体例证语义一致。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":14,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"contrarily"},{"key":"B","text":"consequently"},{"key":"C","text":"similarly"},{"key":"D","text":"simultaneously"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"14.","reason":"前句是家庭结构变化，后句是其后果（监护减少），明显因果 线索就在前后两句的语义关系：前句 More families consist of one-parent households or two working parents 描述家庭结构变化为单亲/双职工，后句 children are likely to have less supervision at home 说明 \"孩子在家所受监护减少\"——后者是前者直接导致的后果，因果关系明显。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"contrarily 表 \"相反地\"，要求后句与前句对立，但 \"监护减少\" 不与 \"单亲/双职工\" 对立，反而是其结果。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"consequently 表 \"因此\"，正好承接前句 \"家庭结构变了\"，引出后句 \"孩子监护减少\" 这一直接后果。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"similarly 用于并列同类现象的比较，但前后两句一个是 \"现象\"、一个是 \"结果\"，并非两个类似现象，逻辑不匹配。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"simultaneously 仅表 \"同时\"，无法揭示前后句的因果关系；本句强调的是后果，而非两个事件同时发生。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":15,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"than"},{"key":"B","text":"that"},{"key":"C","text":"which"},{"key":"D","text":"as"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"语法形态","stemZh":"15.","reason":"空前 less supervision 已锁死 than 比较 线索就在空前的关键词：children are likely to have less supervision at home __(15)__ was common in the traditional family __(16)__.——less 是比较级的标志，紧接其后的连接词必须是 than 才能引导比较对象 \"传统家庭中常见的（监护）\"。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"than 与前文 less supervision 共同构成 \"比……更少的监护\" 比较结构，是该句法的唯一合法连词。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"that 不能用于 less … ___ 比较结构后引导比较项；它只能作宾语从句或定语从句连词，与本结构不匹配。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"which 是关系代词，引导定语从句，与 less … 比较结构语法上不兼容。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"as 用于 as much / as many 等同等比较结构，无法承接 less + 名词 这一不等比较。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":16,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"system"},{"key":"B","text":"structure"},{"key":"C","text":"concept"},{"key":"D","text":"heritage"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"16.","reason":"上下文反复在谈 \"家庭结构变化\"，包括同段开头一句的潜台词 线索见同段一开头 Families have also __(13)__ changes these years. More families consist of one-parent households or two working parents——同段从一开始就在讨论 \"家庭由什么组成、结构如何变化\"，因此 traditional family ___ 应是 traditional family structure（传统家庭结构），与全段主题词 \"结构\" 一致。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"system 指 \"系统、体制\"，传统家庭 system 偏向制度安排，不及 structure 直接对应 \"家庭组成形式\"。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"structure 指 \"结构\"，traditional family structure 即 \"传统家庭结构\"，精准呼应同段开头 More families consist of one-parent households or two working parents 提到的家庭组成变化。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"concept 指 \"概念\"，多用于抽象观念定义，与 \"传统家庭中常见的监护方式\" 这一具体结构语境不符。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"heritage 表 \"遗产、传承\"，带文化沉淀色彩，与本段中性、社会学式描述家庭变化的语气不合。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":17,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"assessable"},{"key":"B","text":"identifiable"},{"key":"C","text":"negligible"},{"key":"D","text":"incredible"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"17.","reason":"include 之后给出三条具体原因，正是 \"可辨识\" 之意 线索见本句中 include 后罗列的三条具体原因：include frustration or failure in school, the increased __(18)__ of drugs and alcohol, and the growing __(19)__ of child abuse and child neglect.——既然作者能列出这些具体原因，那它们必然属于 \"可被识别/可被指认\" 的范畴，所以 causes 的修饰语只能是 identifiable。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"assessable 指 \"可评估的\"，常用于税项、风险量化，搭配 causes 偏离常用语境，且不及 identifiable 直接表 \"可被辨识\"。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"identifiable 表 \"可识别、可辨认的\"，与 include 后罗列的三条具体原因正好对应——既已能被列出，自然是 \"可被识别\" 的成因。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"negligible 表 \"可忽略不计的\"，但作者既然郑重列出这些原因，并指出它们 \"增加犯罪概率\"，显然不可能是 \"可忽略的\"。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"incredible 带 \"难以置信、了不起\" 的口语色彩，与本文严谨综述的语气格格不入。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":18,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"expense"},{"key":"B","text":"restriction"},{"key":"C","text":"allocation"},{"key":"D","text":"availability"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"18.","reason":"本句把 drugs and alcohol 与 child abuse、school failure 并列作为犯罪诱因 线索见本句 Other __(17)__ causes of offensive acts include frustration or failure in school, the increased __(18)__ of drugs and alcohol, and the growing __(19)__ of child abuse and child neglect.——三项并列原因中，毒品酒精成为犯罪诱因的方式是 \"可得性变高/越来越容易获得\"，与下一项 \"虐待/疏忽的发生率上升\" 在 \"现象增加导致犯罪\" 的逻辑上对称。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"expense 指 \"花费\"，increased expense of drugs 意为价格上涨，价格上涨反而会降低犯罪诱因，逻辑相反。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"restriction 指 \"限制\"，increased restriction 表示约束增强，反而抑制毒品酒精消费，与 \"增加犯罪概率\" 的语境相反。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"allocation 指 \"分配、拨款\"，多用于资金、配额等正式分配场景，无法形容毒品酒精的社会可得性。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"availability 指 \"可得性、易得程度\"，increased availability of drugs and alcohol 即 \"毒品和酒精越来越容易获得\"，是导致青少年犯罪概率提升的标准社会学表述。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":19,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"incidence"},{"key":"B","text":"awareness"},{"key":"C","text":"exposure"},{"key":"D","text":"popularity"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"19.","reason":"三项并列原因均为 \"现象增多→犯罪诱因\"，要求与前两项对称 线索仍在本句的并列结构：include frustration or failure in school, the increased __(18)__ of drugs and alcohol, and the growing __(19)__ of child abuse and child neglect.——前两项都是 \"现象增多→犯罪概率上升\" 的语义模板，本空也必须填 \"虐童疏忽事件发生率上升\" 这一同模板表达，因此用 incidence（发生率、事件数）。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"incidence 指 \"发生率、发生频率\"，the growing incidence of child abuse and child neglect 正是 \"虐童与忽视事件发生率上升\"，与犯罪诱因递增的语义吻合。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"awareness 表 \"意识、知晓度\"，意识增强通常引向更好的预防而非更多犯罪，与本句作为犯罪诱因的语义相反。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"exposure 表 \"曝光、媒体暴露\"，强调被公众知晓，但本句强调的是事件本身发生增多，而非媒体曝光率，方向不对。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"popularity 表 \"流行、受欢迎\"，搭配虐童这种负面事件荒谬，绝对不通。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":20,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"provided"},{"key":"B","text":"since"},{"key":"C","text":"although"},{"key":"D","text":"supposing"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"20.","reason":"前是 \"提高犯罪概率\"，后是 \"未确立直接因果\"，二者构成让步 线索就在前后两个分句：All these conditions tend to increase the probability of a child committing a criminal act, __(20)__ a direct causal relationship has not yet been established.——前句肯定 \"这些条件会提高犯罪概率\"，后句却让一步 \"虽然尚未确立直接因果关系\"。这种 \"前肯定 + 后让步\" 的关系正是 although 的语义。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"provided 表 \"假如、只要\"，引出条件，但本句主从句不是 \"在某条件下才成立\"，而是 \"虽然如此但仍然成立\"，逻辑不符。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"since 表 \"既然、因为\"，引出原因，但 \"尚未确立直接因果\" 不是 \"现象增加犯罪概率\" 的原因，方向反了。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"although 表 \"虽然、尽管\"，正好让一步：\"虽然直接因果关系尚未确立，但这些条件依然会提高犯罪概率\"——是学术综述谨慎收束的标准句型，也呼应了 All theories, however, are tentative 的同样基调。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"supposing 表 \"假设、如果\"，引出假想情境，但本句两个分句都是事实陈述（前肯定后让步），并非假设，不匹配。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-1","kind":"reading","title":"Text 1","textNo":1,"directions":"Directions: Read the following four texts. Answer the questions after each text by choosing A, B, C or D. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET . (40 points)","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 1","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-1","text":"Hunting for a job late last year, lawyer Gant Redmon stumbled across CareerBuilder, a job database on the Internet. He searched it with no success but was attracted by the site's \"personal search agent\". It's an interactive feature that lets visitors key in job criteria such as location, title, and salary, then E-mails them when a matching position is posted in the database. Redmon chose the keywords legal, intellectual property and Washington, D.C. Three weeks later, he got his first notification of an opening. \"I struck gold,\" says Redmon, who E-mailed his resume to the employer and won a position as in-house counsel for a company."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-2","text":"With thousands of career-related sites on the Internet, finding promising openings can be time-consuming and inefficient. Search agents reduce the need for repeated visits to the databases. But although a search agent worked for Redmon, career experts see drawbacks. Narrowing your criteria, for example, may work against you: \"Every time you answer a question you eliminate a possibility,\" says one expert."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-3","text":"For any job search, you should start with a narrow concept—what you think you want to do—then broaden it. \"None of these programs do that,\" says another expert. \"There's no career counseling implicit in all of this.\" Instead, the best strategy is to use the agent as a kind of tip service to keep abreast of jobs in a particular database; when you get E-mail, consider it a reminder to check the database again. \"I would not rely on agents for finding everything that is added to a database that might interest me,\" says the author of a job-searching guide."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-4","text":"Some sites design their agents to tempt job hunters to return. When CareerSite's agent sends out messages to those who have signed up for its service, for example, it includes only three potential jobs—those it considers the best matches. There may be more matches in the database; job hunters will have to visit the site again to find them—and they do. \"On the day after we send our messages, we see a sharp increase in our traffic,\" says Seth Peets, vice president of marketing for CareerSite."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-5","text":"Even those who aren't hunting for jobs may find search agents worthwhile. Some use them to keep a close watch on the demand for their line of work or gather information on compensation to arm themselves when negotiating for a raise. Although happily employed, Redmon maintains his agent at CareerBuilder. \"You always keep your eyes open,\" he says. Working with a personal search agent means having another set of eyes looking out for you."}]},"questions":[{"n":21,"stem":"How did Redmon find his job?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"By searching openings in a job database."},{"key":"B","text":"By posting a matching position in a database."},{"key":"C","text":"By using a special service of a database."},{"key":"D","text":"By E-mailing his resume to a database."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"Redmon 是如何找到他的工作的?","choicesZh":{"A":"通过在职位数据库中搜索空缺职位。","B":"通过在数据库中发布匹配职位。","C":"通过使用数据库的特殊服务。","D":"通过将简历用电子邮件发送到数据库。"},"analysis":{"type":"How did Redmon find his job? 以 How 提问、指向具体行为，问的是文中已写明的事实，不是隐含或主旨。","parse":"How did Redmon find his job? 是最朴素的特殊疑问句，主语 Redmon、谓语 find、宾语 his job，无从句、无否定、无比较，零陷阱。","locateEn":"He searched it with no success but was attracted by the site's \"personal search agent\". It's an interactive feature that lets visitors key in job criteria such as location, title, and salary, then E-mails them when a matching position is posted in the database.","locateZh":"他用关键词搜了一遍，毫无所获，但被该站点的「私人搜索代理」吸引。这是一个交互功能，让访客输入工作地点、职位、薪资等条件，当数据库中出现匹配岗位时，会用邮件通知他们。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"By searching openings in a job database. 描述的是普通搜索，而原文写得很清楚他「搜了但没成功」（He searched it with no success），是被 search agent 而非搜索本身救场的。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"By posting a matching position in a database. 把「发布岗位」的动作扣在 Redmon 头上，但原文里发布岗位的是雇主/系统，他是接收方。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判到「靠 personal search agent」后，四项里只有 C 把它抽象成 special service of a database，而 A、B、D 都偏离了这条事实链。","pairs":[{"orig":"was attracted by the site's \"personal search agent\"","opt":"By using a special service of a database."},{"orig":"lets visitors key in job criteria ... then E-mails them when a matching position is posted in the database","opt":"By using a special service of a database."}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"By E-mailing his resume to a database. 是他在 agent 通知到匹配岗位之后做的应聘动作，是结果环节；而题干问的是「如何找到」，对应的是 agent 这一发现机制。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":22,"stem":"Which of the following can be a disadvantage of search agents?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Lack of counseling."},{"key":"B","text":"Limited number of visits."},{"key":"C","text":"Lower efficiency."},{"key":"D","text":"Fewer successful matches."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"以下哪项可能是搜索代理的缺点?","choicesZh":{"A":"缺乏咨询。","B":"访问次数有限。","C":"效率较低。","D":"成功匹配较少。"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following can be a disadvantage of search agents? 让你从四项里挑出文中提到的缺点，答案必在原文，不需推理。","parse":"Which of the following can be a disadvantage of search agents? 主语是 Which，系动词 can be，表语 a disadvantage of search agents，情态动词 can 表「可能是」，不是绝对断言——这意味着只要原文提到 search agents 的某项不足即可，不必是「最大」缺点。","locateEn":"But although a search agent worked for Redmon, career experts see drawbacks. Narrowing your criteria, for example, may work against you: \"Every time you answer a question you eliminate a possibility,\" says one expert.","locateZh":"尽管 search agent 对 Redmon 起了作用，但职业专家看到了它的缺点。比如，把搜索条件收窄反而可能害你：「每回答一个问题就排除一种可能」，一位专家说。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"文章在 2、3 段共给出两个缺点：narrowing 适得其反、no career counseling；其中 no counseling 在第 3 段被用作论证支点，且四个选项里只有 A 与之对应，预判与选项严密咬合。","pairs":[{"orig":"There's no career counseling implicit in all of this.","opt":"Lack of counseling."},{"orig":"But although a search agent worked for Redmon, career experts see drawbacks.","opt":"Lack of counseling."}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Limited number of visits. 把 search agent 描述成「限制访问次数」，原文从未谈过 visits 被 agent 限制；第 2 段反而说 agent reduce the need for repeated visits——是减少访问需要，不是限制访问次数。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Lower efficiency. 与原文事实相反——原文 Search agents reduce the need for repeated visits to the databases. 是说 agent 提高效率，不是降低。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Fewer successful matches. 推断「成功匹配更少」，原文只说 narrowing criteria 会 eliminate possibilities，并没断言最终的「成功匹配数」会变少——可能性减少≠成功数量减少。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":23,"stem":"The expression \"tip service\" (Line 4, Paragraph 3) most probably means.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"advisory."},{"key":"B","text":"compensation."},{"key":"C","text":"interaction."},{"key":"D","text":"reminder."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义句意题","stemZh":"短语\"tip service\"(第3段第4行)最可能的意思是。","choicesZh":{"A":"咨询性的。","B":"补偿。","C":"互动。","D":"提醒。"},"analysis":{"type":"The expression \"tip service\" (Line 4, Paragraph 3) most probably means. 出现 the expression ... most probably means 的固定句式，且把原文短语用引号标出，是最典型的词义题模板。","parse":"The expression \"tip service\" (Line 4, Paragraph 3) most probably means. 是不完整陈述句，待选项续完；most probably 表示「最可能」，提示答案应是上下文逻辑下最贴切的一个，不是绝对唯一。","locateEn":"Instead, the best strategy is to use the agent as a kind of tip service to keep abreast of jobs in a particular database; when you get E-mail, consider it a reminder to check the database again.","locateZh":"最好的策略是把 agent 当作一种「提示服务」来用，以便随时了解某个数据库里的岗位动向；当你收到邮件时，把它当作「再去查一下数据库」的提醒。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"advisory. 译作「咨询/建议」，与原文恰好相反——第 3 段反复强调 There's no career counseling implicit in all of this.，明确说 agent 不做咨询。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"compensation.（报酬/薪酬）与第 3 段语境无关；该词来自第 5 段 gather information on compensation，与 tip service 的语境完全不搭。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"interaction.（互动）与 tip service 的本质不符——agent 发邮件给你属于单向通知，不是双向互动；interaction 这一描述更适合第 1 段的 interactive feature，但本题问的是第 3 段的 tip service。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"作者已经在分号后用 reminder 主动解释了 tip service 的功能；预判一旦走到「提醒回查数据库」，自然就锁 D。","pairs":[{"orig":"consider it a reminder to check the database again","opt":"reminder."}]}}}}},{"n":24,"stem":"Why does CareerSite's agent offer each job hunter only three job options?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"To focus on better job matches."},{"key":"B","text":"To attract more returning visits."},{"key":"C","text":"To reserve space for more messages."},{"key":"D","text":"To increase the rate of success."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"为什么 CareerSite 的代理只为每位求职者提供三个工作选项?","choicesZh":{"A":"为了专注于更好的工作匹配。","B":"为了吸引更多回访。","C":"为了保留更多信息的空间。","D":"为了提高成功率。"},"analysis":{"type":"Why does CareerSite's agent offer each job hunter only three job options? 问的是「为什么只给三个」，原文若直接给出动机句即为细节题；本题作者紧接着给出了动机句，按细节题处理。","parse":"Why does CareerSite's agent offer each job hunter only three job options? 一般疑问语序的特殊疑问句，only three 中 only 表程度限定，提示「只给三个」本身就是动作的反常之处——答案要解释这个反常。","locateEn":"Some sites design their agents to tempt job hunters to return. When CareerSite's agent sends out messages to those who have signed up for its service, for example, it includes only three potential jobs—those it considers the best matches.","locateZh":"一些站点把 agent 设计成「引诱求职者回访」的工具。比如 CareerSite 的 agent 给注册用户发邮件时，只放进它认为最匹配的三个岗位。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"To focus on better job matches. 把「选最匹配的三个」当成目的，原文里 those it considers the best matches 只是「为什么挑这三个」的手段，目的是 tempt job hunters to return。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判到「引诱回访」后，B 项里 attract、returning、visits 三个核心词都能在原文动机句和结果句中找到对应位，逐词都站得住。","pairs":[{"orig":"tempt job hunters to return","opt":"To attract more returning visits."},{"orig":"On the day after we send our messages, we see a sharp increase in our traffic","opt":"To attract more returning visits."}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"To reserve space for more messages. 在文中找不到任何依据，文章既未谈邮件容量也未谈 message 空间限制。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"To increase the rate of success. 把「精挑三个」推到「提高成功率」，原文从未提及任何「成功率」「rate of success」，是从手段（精挑）再推一步的过度推断。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":25,"stem":"Which of the following is true according to the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Personal search agents are indispensable to job-hunters."},{"key":"B","text":"Some sites keep E-mailing job seekers to trace their demands."},{"key":"C","text":"Personal search agents are also helpful to those already employed."},{"key":"D","text":"Some agents stop sending information to people once they are employed."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据文章,以下哪项是正确的?","choicesZh":{"A":"个人搜索代理对求职者来说是不可或缺的。","B":"一些网站持续向求职者发送电子邮件以追踪他们的需求。","C":"个人搜索代理对已就业人员也有帮助。","D":"一些代理一旦人们就业就停止向他们发送信息。"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following is true according to the text? 明确要求 true according to the text，答案必须能在原文找到字面或同义对应，是典型的判断式细节题。","parse":"Which of the following is true according to the text? 万能题干，无修饰陷阱；according to the text 限定了「答案必须出自原文」，不是常识题。","locateEn":"Even those who aren't hunting for jobs may find search agents worthwhile. Some use them to keep a close watch on the demand for their line of work or gather information on compensation to arm themselves when negotiating for a raise.","locateZh":"即便不在求职的人也可能觉得 search agent 值得用——有人用它密切关注本行业的需求，或收集薪酬信息以备加薪谈判时使用。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"Personal search agents are indispensable to job-hunters. 用 indispensable（不可或缺）做绝对断言，原文只说有用、有缺点（career experts see drawbacks），并明确建议不能完全依赖（I would not rely on agents for finding everything）。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Some sites keep E-mailing job seekers to trace their demands. 把第 4 段「站点发邮件吸引回访」的事实换成「为了追踪用户需求」——原文动机是 tempt job hunters to return，不是追踪需求。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"第 5 段从主张句到 Redmon 个例再到总结金句 another set of eyes looking out for you，整段一致论证「已就业者也能用 agent」——C 项是该段的浓缩。","pairs":[{"orig":"Even those who aren't hunting for jobs may find search agents worthwhile","opt":"Personal search agents are also helpful to those already employed."},{"orig":"Although happily employed, Redmon maintains his agent at CareerBuilder.","opt":"Personal search agents are also helpful to those already employed."}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Some agents stop sending information to people once they are employed. 与第 5 段事实完全相反——Although happily employed, Redmon maintains his agent at CareerBuilder. 明示已就业者 agent 仍在持续工作。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-2","kind":"reading","title":"Text 2","textNo":2,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 2","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-1","text":"Over the past century, all kinds of unfairness and discrimination have been condemned or made illegal. But one insidious form continues to thrive: alphabetism. This, for those as yet unaware of such a disadvantage, refers to discrimination against those whose surnames begin with a letter in the lower half of the alphabet."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-2","text":"It has long been known that a taxi firm called AAAA cars has a big advantage over Zodiac cars when customers thumb through their phone directories. Less well known is the advantage that Adam Abbott has in life over Zoë Zysman. English names are fairly evenly spread between the halves of the alphabet. Yet a suspiciously large number of top people have surnames beginning with letters between A and K."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-3","text":"Thus the American president and vice-president have surnames starting with B and C respectively; and 26 of George Bush's predecessors (including his father) had surnames in the first half of the alphabet against just 16 in the second half. Even more striking, six of the seven heads of government of the G7 rich countries are alphabetically advantaged (Berlusconi, Blair, Bush, Chirac, Chrétien and Koizumi). The world's three top central bankers (Greenspan, Duisenberg and Hayami) are all close to the top of the alphabet, even if one of them really uses Japanese characters. As are the world's five richest men (Gates, Buffett, Allen, Ellison and Albrecht)."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-4","text":"Can this merely be coincidence? One theory, dreamt up in all the spare time enjoyed by the alphabetically disadvantaged, is that the rot sets in early. At the start of the first year in infant school, teachers seat pupils alphabetically from the front, to make it easier to remember their names. So short-sighted Zysman junior gets stuck in the back row, and is rarely asked the improving questions posed by those insensitive teachers. At the time the alphabetically disadvantaged may think they have had a lucky escape. Yet the result may be worse qualifications, because they get less individual attention, as well as less confidence in speaking publicly."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-5","text":"The humiliation continues. At university graduation ceremonies, the ABCs proudly get their awards first; by the time they reach the Zysmans most people are literally having a ZZZ. Shortlists for job interviews, election ballot papers, lists of conference speakers and attendees: all tend to be drawn up alphabetically, and their recipients lose interest as they plough through them."}]},"questions":[{"n":26,"stem":"What does the author intend to illustrate with AAAA cars and Zodiac cars?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A kind of overlooked inequality."},{"key":"B","text":"A type of conspicuous bias."},{"key":"C","text":"A type of personal prejudice."},{"key":"D","text":"A kind of brand discrimination."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"例证目的题","stemZh":"作者想通过 AAAA 汽车和 Zodiac 汽车说明什么?","choicesZh":{"A":"一种被忽视的不平等","B":"一种明显的偏见","C":"一种个人成见","D":"一种品牌歧视"},"analysis":{"type":"What does the author intend to illustrate with AAAA cars and Zodiac cars? 直接问作者「想用这两个例子说明什么」，符合例证目的题的典型句式。","parse":"What does the author intend to illustrate with AAAA cars and Zodiac cars? 是常规特殊疑问句，主干为 What does the author intend to illustrate，with 短语表示「用…来说明」，没有任何陷阱结构。","locateEn":"It has long been known that a taxi firm called AAAA cars has a big advantage over Zodiac cars when customers thumb through their phone directories. Less well known is the advantage that Adam Abbott has in life over Zoë Zysman.","locateZh":"众所周知，一家叫 AAAA 的出租车公司在顾客翻电话簿时比叫 Zodiac 的公司大占便宜；而不那么广为人知的是，亚当·阿博特在人生中也比佐伊·齐斯曼占便宜。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"AAAA/Zodiac 是众所周知的不公，Adam/Zoë 是鲜为人知的不公，作者用前者反衬后者，意在揭示这一被忽视的不平等，与 A kind of overlooked inequality 完全吻合。","pairs":[{"orig":"But one insidious form continues to thrive: alphabetism","opt":"A kind of overlooked inequality"},{"orig":"Less well known is the advantage that Adam Abbott has in life over Zoë Zysman","opt":"A kind of overlooked inequality"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"A type of conspicuous bias 中 conspicuous（显眼的）与原文 insidious 与 Less well known 正相反，方向完全颠倒。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"A type of personal prejudice 中 personal（个人的）暗示是个体偏见；原文谈的是社会层面的系统性歧视（涉及总统、富豪等群体），范围被缩窄。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"A kind of brand discrimination（品牌歧视）只对应 AAAA/Zodiac 公司例的字面，忽略了 Less well known is the advantage that Adam Abbott has in life over Zoë Zysman 这层人姓氏的真正论点。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":27,"stem":"What can we infer from the first three paragraphs?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"In both East and West, names are essential to success."},{"key":"B","text":"The alphabet is to blame for the failure of Zoë Zysman."},{"key":"C","text":"Customers often pay a lot of attention to companies' names."},{"key":"D","text":"Some form of discrimination is too subtle to recognize."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"推断题","stemZh":"从前三段我们可以推断出什么?","choicesZh":{"A":"在东西方,姓名对成功都至关重要","B":"字母表应该为 Zoë Zysman 的失败负责","C":"顾客经常很关注公司的名称","D":"某些形式的歧视过于微妙而难以识别"},"analysis":{"type":"What can we infer from the first three paragraphs? 完全符合推断题的标准句式。","parse":"What can we infer from the first three paragraphs? 句式简单，from 短语指明推断的依据范围，无理解障碍。","locateEn":"Less well known is the advantage that Adam Abbott has in life over Zoë Zysman.","locateZh":"不太为人所知的是，Adam Abbott 在生活中相对 Zoë Zysman 所拥有的优势。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文只举了美国总统、G7、富豪等西方例子，even if one of them really uses Japanese characters 是一句轻描淡写的让步，并未支持「名字对东西方都至关重要」。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"The alphabet is to blame for the failure of Zoë Zysman 中 failure（失败）远比原文 less … advantage（占便宜较少）严重，且 to blame for（归咎于）把相关性升级为因果责任。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Customers often pay a lot of attention to companies' names 只覆盖 a taxi firm called AAAA cars 一个例子，且原文是 thumb through phone directories（翻名录），并不能推出「顾客重视公司名」这一普遍结论。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"正确项 = 把前三段的核心事实「这种歧视存在却被忽视」抽象成「歧视太隐蔽以至于难以识别」，正是一步延伸，符合推断题作答规范。","pairs":[{"orig":"one insidious form continues to thrive: alphabetism","opt":"Some form of discrimination is too subtle to recognize"},{"orig":"for those as yet unaware of such a disadvantage","opt":"too subtle to recognize"}]}}}}},{"n":28,"stem":"The 4th paragraph suggests that_____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"questions are often put to the more intelligent students"},{"key":"B","text":"alphabetically disadvantaged students often escape from class"},{"key":"C","text":"teachers should pay attention to all of their students"},{"key":"D","text":"students should be seated according to their eyesight"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"推断题","stemZh":"第四段表明_____","choicesZh":{"A":"问题经常被提给更聪明的学生","B":"按字母顺序处于不利地位的学生经常逃课","C":"教师应该关注所有学生","D":"学生应该根据视力安排座位"},"analysis":{"type":"The 4th paragraph suggests that 是补全句结构，配合 suggests 判为推断题。","parse":"The 4th paragraph suggests that_____. 是「主语+suggests+that 从句」的补全句，选项即从句内容，下笔时把选项整句嫁接到 suggests 之后即可。","locateEn":"So short-sighted Zysman junior gets stuck in the back row, and is rarely asked the improving questions posed by those insensitive teachers. … Yet the result may be worse qualifications, because they get less individual attention, as well as less confidence in speaking publicly.","locateZh":"于是近视的小齐斯曼被困在最后一排，那些不敏感的教师极少向他提出有助于进步的问题……结果可能是更差的学业表现，因为他们得到的个体关注更少，公开表达的自信也更弱。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文只说前排学生因座位被多提问，从未说他们「更聪明」；questions are often put to the more intelligent students 中的 more intelligent 凭空添加。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"alphabetically disadvantaged students often escape from class 中 escape from class（逃课）字面误导自 At the time the alphabetically disadvantaged may think they have had a lucky escape——原文意为「以为逃过一劫」，并非「逃课」。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"段落只描述了「老师忽视后排学生造成不公」的负面事实，按 suggests 的题型要求，作答应是它隐含的正面应然——老师应当关注所有学生。","pairs":[{"orig":"those insensitive teachers","opt":"teachers should pay attention to all of their students"},{"orig":"they get less individual attention","opt":"pay attention to all of their students"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"students should be seated according to their eyesight 抓住了 short-sighted Zysman junior 这个修饰性细节，并将其升格为段意建议，与作者真实意图不符。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":29,"stem":"What does the author mean by \"most people are literally having a ZZZ\" (Lines 2-3, Paragraph 5)?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"They are getting impatient."},{"key":"B","text":"They are noisily dozing off."},{"key":"C","text":"They are feeling humiliated."},{"key":"D","text":"They are busy with word puzzles."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义句意题","stemZh":"作者所说的\"大多数人实际上正在 ZZZ\"(第五段第2-3行)是什么意思?","choicesZh":{"A":"他们正变得不耐烦","B":"他们正吵闹地打瞌睡","C":"他们感到羞辱","D":"他们正忙于字谜游戏"},"analysis":{"type":"What does the author mean by 加上引号短语，是词义句意题的固定形态。","parse":"What does the author mean by \"most people are literally having a ZZZ\" 中 literally 修饰 having a ZZZ，ZZZ 是漫画里表示打瞌睡的拟声符号，理解为「字面意义上在打呼噜」即可。","locateEn":"At university graduation ceremonies, the ABCs proudly get their awards first; by the time they reach the Zysmans most people are literally having a ZZZ.","locateZh":"在大学毕业典礼上，姓氏 ABC 字母的人率先骄傲地领奖；等念到齐斯曼们的时候，多数人已经在打呼噜了。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"They are getting impatient（不耐烦）只是 dozing off（已睡着）的前一步状态，原文 literally having a ZZZ 强调「真的在打呼噜」，已经越过不耐烦。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"从拟声修辞 ZZZ 还原为字面动作即 noisily dozing off，与上下文「典礼冗长、听众失去注意力」吻合。","pairs":[{"orig":"most people are literally having a ZZZ","opt":"They are noisily dozing off"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"They are feeling humiliated 中 humiliated（感到羞辱）对应的是 The humiliation continues 的句子，但那是描述「被忽视的 Zysmans」的处境，不是 ZZZ 句的语义。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"They are busy with word puzzles（在玩字谜）字面联想 ZZZ 像字谜里的符号，但原文从未提及字谜，是凭空臆造。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":30,"stem":"Which of the following is true according to the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"People with surnames beginning with N to Z are often ill-treated."},{"key":"B","text":"VIPs in the Western world gain a great deal from alphabetism."},{"key":"C","text":"The campaign to eliminate alphabetism still has a long way to go."},{"key":"D","text":"Putting things alphabetically may lead to unintentional bias."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据文章,下列哪项是正确的?","choicesZh":{"A":"姓氏以 N 到 Z 开头的人经常受到虐待","B":"西方世界的重要人物从字母排序主义中获益良多","C":"消除字母排序主义的运动仍然任重道远","D":"按字母顺序排列事物可能导致无意的偏见"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following is true according to the text? 强调「与原文一致」，属于细节判断而非推断。","parse":"Which of the following is true according to the text? 是常规筛选式问句，according to the text 限定判定依据为原文字面信息，不容外延。","locateEn":"Shortlists for job interviews, election ballot papers, lists of conference speakers and attendees: all tend to be drawn up alphabetically, and their recipients lose interest as they plough through them.","locateZh":"面试入围名单、选举选票、会议发言人及与会者名单——这些通常都按字母顺序列出，收到名单的人在翻阅时逐渐失去兴趣。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"People with surnames beginning with N to Z are often ill-treated 中 ill-treated（被虐待）远比原文 lose interest、less individual attention 严重，且 often 把「可能/偶有」升格为「经常」。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"VIPs in the Western world gain a great deal from alphabetism 暗示名人靠字母表歧视获益甚多；但原文只是观察到名人多姓 A~K 的相关性，Can this merely be coincidence? 表明作者也只是提出疑问，未定因果。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"The campaign to eliminate alphabetism still has a long way to go 中 campaign（运动）原文从未提及；文中没有任何反对字母表歧视的运动，纯属虚构。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"D 用 may（程度词温和）+ unintentional（无意识）+ bias（偏向），三处都与全文措辞精确对应，是最稳的真陈述。","pairs":[{"orig":"all tend to be drawn up alphabetically, and their recipients lose interest as they plough through them","opt":"Putting things alphabetically may lead to unintentional bias"},{"orig":"teachers seat pupils alphabetically from the front, to make it easier to remember their names","opt":"may lead to unintentional bias"}]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-3","kind":"reading","title":"Text 3","textNo":3,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 3","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-1","text":"When it comes to the slowing economy, Ellen Spero isn't biting her nails just yet. But the 47-year-old manicurist isn't cutting, filing or polishing as many nails as she'd like to, either. Most of her clients spend $12 to $50 weekly, but last month two longtime customers suddenly stopped showing up. Spero blames the softening economy. \"I'm a good economic indicator,\" she says. \"I provide a service that people can do without when they're concerned about saving some dollars.\" So Spero is downscaling, shopping at middle-brow Dillard's department store near her suburban Cleveland home, instead of Neiman Marcus. \"I don't know if other clients are going to abandon me, too,\" she says."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-2","text":"Even before Alan Greenspan's admission that America's red-hot economy is cooling, lots of working folks had already seen signs of the slowdown themselves. From car dealerships to Gap outlets, sales have been lagging for months as shoppers temper their spending. For retailers, who last year took in 24 percent of their revenue between Thanksgiving and Christmas, the cautious approach is coming at a crucial time. Already, experts say, holiday sales are off 7 percent from last year's pace. But don't sound any alarms just yet. Consumers seem only mildly concerned, not panicked, and many say they remain optimistic about the economy's long-term prospects even as they do some modest belt-tightening."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-3","text":"Consumers say they're not in despair because, despite the dreadful headlines, their own fortunes still feel pretty good. Home prices are holding steady in most regions. In Manhattan, \"there's a new gold rush happening in the $4 million to $10 million range, predominantly fed by Wall Street bonuses,\" says broker Barbara Corcoran. In San Francisco, prices are still rising even as frenzied overbidding quiets. \"Instead of 20 to 30 offers, now maybe you only get two or three,\" says John Tealdi, a Bay Area real-estate broker. And most folks still feel pretty comfortable about their ability to find and keep a job."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-4","text":"Many folks see silver linings to this slowdown. Potential home buyers would cheer for lower interest rates. Employers wouldn't mind a few fewer bubbles in the job market. Many consumers seem to have been influenced by stock-market swings, which investors now view as a necessary ingredient to a sustained boom. Diners might see an upside, too. Getting a table at Manhattan's hot new Alain Ducasse restaurant used to be impossible. Not anymore. For that, Greenspan & Co. may still be worth toasting."}]},"questions":[{"n":31,"stem":"By \"Ellen Spero isn't biting her nails just yet\" (Line 1, Paragraph 1), the author means_____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Spero can hardly maintain her business."},{"key":"B","text":"Spero is too much engaged in her work."},{"key":"C","text":"Spero has grown out of her bad habit."},{"key":"D","text":"Spero is not in a desperate situation."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义句意题","stemZh":"作者说\"Ellen Spero 还没有咬指甲\"(第1段第1行)是指_____。","choicesZh":{"A":"Spero 几乎无法维持她的生意。","B":"Spero 过于专注于她的工作。","C":"Spero 已经改掉了她的坏习惯。","D":"Spero 没有处于绝望的境地。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 By \"Ellen Spero isn't biting her nails just yet\" ... the author means 明确要求解释一句话的含义，是典型的句意理解题。","parse":"主句框架是 the author means_____，前面 By \"Ellen Spero isn't biting her nails just yet\" 是介词短语作状语，告诉你要解释的对象。bite one's nails 是英语固定表达，意为「焦虑、紧张到咬指甲」，just yet 表「现在还没」。整句直译：作者所说「她还没咬指甲呢」是什么意思——结构无陷阱，关键是认出 bite one's nails 的比喻义。","locateEn":"When it comes to the slowing economy, Ellen Spero isn't biting her nails just yet. But the 47-year-old manicurist isn't cutting, filing or polishing as many nails as she'd like to, either.","locateZh":"谈到经济减速时，Ellen Spero 还不至于焦虑到咬指甲。但这位 47 岁的美甲师，也没能像她希望的那样修剪、锉磨、抛光那么多指甲。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"Spero can hardly maintain her business 说她「几乎维持不下去生意」，比原文 isn't cutting ... as many nails as she'd like to（少做了点）严重得多。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Spero is too much engaged in her work 把「咬指甲」字面理解成「忙得没空咬」=「太投入工作」，与原文经济减速、客户流失的语境完全相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Spero has grown out of her bad habit 说她「戒掉了咬指甲这个坏习惯」，把 bite nails 当成本人真实的坏习惯处理，原文从未把它当作 Spero 的个人习惯，全文也未谈「戒习惯」。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判核心是「还没到绝望」，四个选项中只有 Spero is not in a desperate situation 在此维度上对应。","pairs":[{"orig":"isn't biting her nails just yet","opt":"Spero is not in a desperate situation"}]}}}}},{"n":32,"stem":"How do the public feel about the current economic situation?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Optimistic."},{"key":"B","text":"Confused."},{"key":"C","text":"Carefree."},{"key":"D","text":"Panicked."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"公众对当前经济形势有何感受?","choicesZh":{"A":"乐观的。","B":"困惑的。","C":"无忧无虑的。","D":"恐慌的。"},"analysis":{"type":"How do the public feel about the current economic situation 问的是原文已陈述的事实——公众情绪——而非作者推断，是细节题。","parse":"How 引导特殊疑问，about the current economic situation 作介词短语状语限定范围。句式平铺直叙，无陷阱——只要分清「当前」和「长期」即可。","locateEn":"Consumers seem only mildly concerned, not panicked, and many say they remain optimistic about the economy's long-term prospects even as they do some modest belt-tightening.","locateZh":"消费者似乎只是轻微担忧、并不恐慌，许多人说，即便在适度勒紧裤腰带，他们对经济的长期前景仍然乐观。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判与选项 Optimistic 在词形与极性上完全对齐，not panicked 也同时排除了同选项中表恐慌/混乱的对照项。","pairs":[{"orig":"they remain optimistic about the economy's long-term prospects","opt":"Optimistic"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Confused 指「困惑、搞不清」，但原文 Consumers seem only mildly concerned, not panicked, and many say they remain optimistic 表达的是清醒的「轻担忧 + 仍乐观」，从未呈现「不知所措」。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Carefree 意为「无忧无虑」，强度上完全超过 only mildly concerned 与 modest belt-tightening——原文显然仍有担忧，并非无忧。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Panicked 直接被原文 not panicked 否定，这是字面级反义。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":33,"stem":"When mentioning \"the $4 million to $10 million range\"(Lines 3, Paragraph 3), the author is talking about _____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"gold market."},{"key":"B","text":"real estate."},{"key":"C","text":"stock exchange."},{"key":"D","text":"venture investment."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义句意题","stemZh":"当提到\"400万至1000万美元区间\"(第3段第3行)时,作者谈论的是_____","choicesZh":{"A":"黄金市场。","B":"房地产。","C":"股票交易。","D":"风险投资。"},"analysis":{"type":"the author is talking about 要求识别该数字所指代的真实领域，本质是「这串数字背后讲的是什么」的指代题/词义题。","parse":"主句 the author is talking about ___，前置 When mentioning ... 是分词状语标明语境。结构简单，重点在判断 $4 million-$10 million 这个金额所属的语义场（房价？股价？金价？）。","locateEn":"In Manhattan, \"there's a new gold rush happening in the $4 million to $10 million range, predominantly fed by Wall Street bonuses,\" says broker Barbara Corcoran.","locateZh":"在曼哈顿，「在 400 万到 1000 万美元价位段正出现新一轮『淘金热』，主要靠华尔街的奖金推动，」房地产经纪人 Barbara Corcoran 说。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"gold market 把 gold rush 字面理解为「黄金市场」，但原文的 gold rush 是 19 世纪美国「淘金热」演化来的英语习语，比喻「为某种机会蜂拥而上」，此处比喻抢购曼哈顿豪宅。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"段首房价主题与 broker 身份双重锁死，gold rush 在此只是比喻房产抢购，不是真金。","pairs":[{"orig":"Home prices are holding steady in most regions","opt":"real estate"},{"orig":"says broker Barbara Corcoran","opt":"real estate"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"stock exchange 借 Wall Street 制造迷惑，但原文 predominantly fed by Wall Street bonuses 只说华尔街的奖金推动了豪宅购买，主题仍是房产、不是股票交易本身。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"venture investment 指「风险投资」，原文第 3 段从未谈及风投，更没把 $4M-$10M 与 venture 任何形式关联。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":34,"stem":"Why can many people see \"silver linings\" to the economic slowdown?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"They would benefit in certain ways."},{"key":"B","text":"The stock market shows signs of recovery."},{"key":"C","text":"Such a slowdown usually precedes a boom."},{"key":"D","text":"The purchasing power would be enhanced."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"为什么许多人能看到经济放缓的\"一线希望\"?","choicesZh":{"A":"他们会在某些方面受益。","B":"股市显示出复苏迹象。","C":"这种放缓通常预示着繁荣。","D":"购买力会增强。"},"analysis":{"type":"Why can many people see \"silver linings\" 问原文给出的具体理由，属对原文具体陈述的复述，是细节题。","parse":"Why 引导原因问句，see silver linings to the economic slowdown 是「在 X 中看到一线光明」的英语习语化表达。结构简单，重点是别被 silver linings 的字面「银色」误导成金属或贵金属。","locateEn":"Many folks see silver linings to this slowdown. Potential home buyers would cheer for lower interest rates. Employers wouldn't mind a few fewer bubbles in the job market.","locateZh":"许多人在这次经济减速中看到了「一线光明」。潜在购房者会为更低的利率欢呼。雇主也不介意就业市场少一些泡沫。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判要求两件事——主语是「人」、谓语是「受益」，仅 A 同时具备。","pairs":[{"orig":"Many folks see silver linings to this slowdown","opt":"They would benefit in certain ways"},{"orig":"Potential home buyers would cheer for lower interest rates","opt":"They would benefit in certain ways"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"The stock market shows signs of recovery 说「股市出现复苏迹象」，但原文 Many consumers seem to have been influenced by stock-market swings, which investors now view as a necessary ingredient to a sustained boom 说的是「股市波动被视为长期繁荣的必要成分」，并未说股市正在复苏；且这只是 silver linings 列举中的一支，不能解释「为何 many people see silver linings」。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Such a slowdown usually precedes a boom 称「这种减速通常预示一次繁荣」，但原文只把 swings 视为 a necessary ingredient to a sustained boom（持续繁荣的必要因素），并未做「减速 → 繁荣」的时间前后/因果断言。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"The purchasing power would be enhanced 说「购买力将被增强」，但原文谈的是「利率下降让购房者高兴、餐厅订位更容易」，从未推到「整体购买力上升」；甚至第 2 段 modest belt-tightening 反向暗示购买力在收紧。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":35,"stem":"To which of the following is the author likely to agree?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A new boom, on the horizon."},{"key":"B","text":"Tighten the belt, the single remedy."},{"key":"C","text":"Caution all right, panic not."},{"key":"D","text":"The more ventures, the more chances."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"作者可能同意以下哪项?","choicesZh":{"A":"新的繁荣即将到来。","B":"勒紧腰带是唯一的补救措施。","C":"谨慎可以,恐慌大可不必。","D":"冒险越多,机会越多。"},"analysis":{"type":"To which of the following is the author likely to agree 要求选作者最赞同的总判断，本质是用一句话概括全文立场，是主旨/态度题。","parse":"倒装结构：正常语序是 The author is likely to agree to which of the following，把介宾 to which... 提前以形成 Wh- 问句。理解上无陷阱，但要意识到选项是四个高度浓缩的标题式短句，需要逐项比对全文立场。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"A new boom, on the horizon 说「新一轮繁荣就在眼前」，但原文 investors now view as a necessary ingredient to a sustained boom 只把股市波动视作「持续繁荣的必要成分」，远未说「繁荣已在地平线」；且全文主调是「减速」，不是「繁荣到来」。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Tighten the belt, the single remedy 说「勒紧腰带是唯一办法」，原文虽有 modest belt-tightening，但用 modest 限定为「适度」，并且只是消费者反应的一个侧面，从未称之为「唯一良方」。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"全文调性是「谨慎」与「不必恐慌」的并列，仅 Caution all right, panic not 同时收纳这两层。","pairs":[{"orig":"Consumers seem only mildly concerned, not panicked","opt":"Caution all right, panic not"},{"orig":"But don't sound any alarms just yet","opt":"Caution all right, panic not"},{"orig":"Many folks see silver linings to this slowdown","opt":"Caution all right, panic not"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"The more ventures, the more chances 说「越冒险越有机会」，原文从未鼓励冒险投资，反而第 4 段 Employers wouldn't mind a few fewer bubbles in the job market 暗含「泡沫减少是好事」——与「鼓励冒险」相反。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-4","kind":"reading","title":"Text 4","textNo":4,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 4","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-1","text":"Americans today don't place a very high value on intellect. Our heroes are athletes, entertainers, and entrepreneurs, not scholars. Even our schools are where we send our children to get a practical education—not to pursue knowledge for the sake of knowledge. Symptoms of pervasive anti-intellectualism in our schools aren't difficult to find."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-2","text":"\"Schools have always been in a society where practical is more important than intellectual,\" says education writer Diane Ravitch. \"Schools could be a counterbalance.\" Ravitch's latest book, Left Back: A Century of Failed School Reforms, traces the roots of anti-intellectualism in our schools, concluding they are anything but a counterbalance to the American distaste for intellectual pursuits."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-3","text":"But they could and should be. Encouraging kids to reject the life of the mind leaves them vulnerable to exploitation and control. Without the ability to think critically, to defend their ideas and understand the ideas of others, they cannot fully participate in our democracy. Continuing along this path, says writer Earl Shorris, \"We will become a second-rate country. We will have a less civil society.\""},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-4","text":"\"Intellect is resented as a form of power or privilege,\" writes historian and professor Richard Hofstadter in Anti-intellectualism in American Life, a Pulitzer-Prize winning book on the roots of anti-intellectualism in US politics, religion, and education. From the beginning of our history, says Hofstadter, our democratic and populist urges have driven us to reject anything that smells of elitism. Practicality, common sense, and native intelligence have been considered more noble qualities than anything you could learn from a book."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-5","text":"Ralph Waldo Emerson and other Transcendentalist philosophers thought schooling and rigorous book learning put unnatural restraints on children: \"We are shut up in schools and college recitation rooms for 10 or 15 years and come out at last with a bellyful of words and do not know a thing.\" Mark Twain's Huckleberry Finn exemplified American anti-intellectualism. Its hero avoids being civilized—going to school and learning to read—so he can preserve his innate goodness."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-6","text":"Intellect, according to Hofstadter, is different from native intelligence, a quality we reluctantly admire. Intellect is the critical, creative, and contemplative side of the mind. Intelligence seeks to grasp, manipulate, re-order, and adjust, while intellect examines, ponders, wonders, theorizes, criticizes, and imagines."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-7","text":"School remains a place where intellect is mistrusted. Hofstadter says our country's educational system is in the grips of people who \"joyfully and militantly proclaim their hostility to intellect and their eagerness to identify with children who show the least intellectual promise.\""}]},"questions":[{"n":36,"stem":"What do American parents expect their children to acquire in school?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The habit of thinking independently."},{"key":"B","text":"Profound knowledge of the world."},{"key":"C","text":"Practical abilities for future career."},{"key":"D","text":"The confidence in intellectual pursuits."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"美国父母期望他们的孩子在学校获得什么?","choicesZh":{"A":"独立思考的习惯。","B":"对世界的深刻认识。","C":"未来职业所需的实用能力。","D":"对智力追求的信心。"},"analysis":{"type":"What do American parents expect their children to acquire in school? 是一个 what 实义问句，问的是文中明确陈述的具体内容，没有 infer/imply/suggest 之类的推理标志。","parse":"主干是 What do American parents expect their children to acquire in school，宾语从句是 expect + 宾语 their children + to do 不定式 acquire，疑问词 what 是 acquire 的宾语前置；结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"Even our schools are where we send our children to get a practical education—not to pursue knowledge for the sake of knowledge.","locateZh":"甚至我们的学校都是我们送孩子去接受实用教育的地方——不是去为了知识本身而追求知识。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"The habit of thinking independently 是作者在第三段 Without the ability to think critically, to defend their ideas and understand the ideas of others, they cannot fully participate in our democracy. 中倡导的能力，并非美国家长当下对孩子的期望。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Profound knowledge of the world 正对应原文被否定的 pursue knowledge for the sake of knowledge，把家长本不期望的内容当作期望，倾向相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判要的是 \"实用层面的所得\"，四个选项中只有 Practical abilities for future career 保留了原文 practical 的核心语义，其余三项均不与 practical education 对应。","pairs":[{"orig":"practical education","opt":"Practical abilities for future career"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"The confidence in intellectual pursuits 在原文中无对应——文章只说美国不重视 intellect，没有任何句子说家长期望孩子获得对 intellectual pursuits 的信心。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":37,"stem":"We can learn from the text that Americans have a history of_____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"undervaluing intellect."},{"key":"B","text":"favoring intellectualism."},{"key":"C","text":"supporting school reform."},{"key":"D","text":"suppressing native intelligence."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"我们可以从文中了解到美国人有_____的历史。","choicesZh":{"A":"低估智力。","B":"推崇智识主义。","C":"支持学校改革。","D":"压制天生的智慧。"},"analysis":{"type":"We can learn from the text that Americans have a history of_____. 用 we can learn from the text 而非 infer/imply，问的是文中已点明、可直接读出的判断，仍属细节范畴。","parse":"主句 We can learn from the text + that 引导的宾语从句 Americans have a history of_____，空格作介词 of 的宾语，应填名词或动名词性短语；结构简单，无陷阱。","locateEn":"From the beginning of our history, says Hofstadter, our democratic and populist urges have driven us to reject anything that smells of elitism.","locateZh":"Hofstadter 说，从我们历史的开端起，我们的民主与平民主义冲动就驱使我们排斥一切带有精英气息的东西。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"undervaluing intellect 同时锁住 \"历史悠久\" 与 \"轻视智识\" 两个语义要素，正与定位段的两条线索吻合。","pairs":[{"orig":"Intellect is resented as a form of power or privilege","opt":"undervaluing intellect"},{"orig":"From the beginning of our history","opt":"undervaluing intellect"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"favoring intellectualism 与原文 Americans today don't place a very high value on intellect 及 Intellect is resented 直接相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文虽提及 Left Back: A Century of Failed School Reforms，但这是一本批判校改失败的书，并非美国人 \"支持校改\" 的证据；以书名诱选。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"suppressing native intelligence 与 native intelligence have been considered more noble qualities than anything you could learn from a book 相反——原文恰是说本能型才智被推崇，而非被压制。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":38,"stem":"The views of Ravitch and Emerson on schooling are_____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"identical."},{"key":"B","text":"similar."},{"key":"C","text":"complementary."},{"key":"D","text":"opposite."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"Ravitch和Emerson关于教育的观点是_____。","choicesZh":{"A":"完全相同的。","B":"相似的。","C":"互补的。","D":"相反的。"},"analysis":{"type":"The views of Ravitch and Emerson on schooling are_____. 用 are 直接问两人观点的关系，选项是 identical/similar/complementary/opposite 四种关系判断，本质是细节比对。","parse":"主语 The views of Ravitch and Emerson on schooling 是 N+of+N+on+N 的多层后置修饰，of 限定 views 的归属、on 限定 views 的议题；系动词 are 后接空格表两人观点关系；理解关键是看清两个后置修饰各自的范围。","locateEn":"\"Schools have always been in a society where practical is more important than intellectual,\" says education writer Diane Ravitch. \"Schools could be a counterbalance.\"","locateZh":"教育作家戴安·拉维奇说：「学校始终处在一个实用重于才智的社会里，学校本可以成为一种制衡力量。」","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"identical 暗指两人观点完全相同，但 Ravitch 想强化学校作用、Emerson 想削弱乃至摆脱学校束缚，二者完全不一致。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"similar 试图把对立立场弱化为 \"相似\"，但 bellyful of words and do not know a thing 与 Schools could be a counterbalance. 在态度极性上反向，无相似可言。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"complementary 指两人观点能在不同维度互补成完整论述，但 Ravitch 与 Emerson 是在同一议题 schooling 上正反对垒，不构成互补。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Ravitch 想让学校制衡反智、即希望学校发挥正面作用；Emerson 把学校描述成束缚孩子、十几年学不到东西的地方，立场针锋相对，唯有 opposite 与之相符。","pairs":[{"orig":"Schools could be a counterbalance.","opt":"opposite"},{"orig":"We are shut up in schools and college recitation rooms for 10 or 15 years and come out at last with a bellyful of words and do not know a thing.","opt":"opposite"}]}}}}},{"n":39,"stem":"Emerson, according to the text, is probably_____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"a pioneer of education reform."},{"key":"B","text":"an opponent of intellectualism."},{"key":"C","text":"a scholar in favor of intellect."},{"key":"D","text":"an advocate of regular schooling."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"推断题","stemZh":"根据文章,Emerson很可能是_____。","choicesZh":{"A":"教育改革的先驱。","B":"智识主义的反对者。","C":"支持智力的学者。","D":"常规学校教育的倡导者。"},"analysis":{"type":"Emerson, according to the text, is probably_____. 的 probably 是典型推断信号——答案不在原文字面，需要从 Emerson 的原话作一步逻辑延伸。","parse":"题干主干为 Emerson, according to the text, is probably_____，其中 according to the text 是插入语，限定这一判断的依据来自文本；is 后缺表语，选项以名词短语形式回填；插入语让句子看似复杂，去掉后结构极简，无其他语法陷阱。","locateEn":"Ralph Waldo Emerson and other Transcendentalist philosophers thought schooling and rigorous book learning put unnatural restraints on children: \"We are shut up in schools and college recitation rooms for 10 or 15 years and come out at last with a bellyful of words and do not know a thing.\"","locateZh":"拉尔夫·瓦尔多·爱默生和其他超验主义哲学家认为学校教育和严苛的书本学习对孩子施加了不自然的束缚：\"我们被关在学校和大学背诵教室里十年十五年，最后出来满肚子词句却一无所知。\"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"a pioneer of education reform 在原文无支撑——Emerson 在文中是反对学校教育的哲学家，不是教育改革的先驱。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Emerson 反对学校教育与书本学习，又被作者放进 anti-intellectualism 的论证段落中举证，由此可一步延伸为 \"反智主义的反对者\"——即 intellectualism 的反对者。","pairs":[{"orig":"schooling and rigorous book learning put unnatural restraints on children","opt":"an opponent of intellectualism"},{"orig":"Mark Twain's Huckleberry Finn exemplified American anti-intellectualism","opt":"an opponent of intellectualism"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"a scholar in favor of intellect 把 Emerson 反智的立场翻转为支持智识者，与 schooling and rigorous book learning put unnatural restraints on children 直接相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"an advocate of regular schooling 把 Emerson 描绘成常规学校教育的拥护者，但 We are shut up in schools and college recitation rooms for 10 or 15 years and come out at last with a bellyful of words and do not know a thing. 显示他是常规学校教育的强烈反对者。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":40,"stem":"What does the author think of intellect?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It is second to intelligence."},{"key":"B","text":"It evolves from common sense."},{"key":"C","text":"It is to be pursued."},{"key":"D","text":"It underlies power."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"态度题","stemZh":"作者对智力持什么看法?","choicesZh":{"A":"它次于智慧。","B":"它从常识演化而来。","C":"它值得追求。","D":"它是权力的基础。"},"analysis":{"type":"What does the author think of intellect? 用 think of 直接问作者对某对象的看法，是态度题的标准句式。","parse":"主干 What does the author think of intellect? 是 think of sth. 的提问结构，what 作 think of 的宾语前置；句式简单，关键是 think of 等于 have what opinion of。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"It is second to intelligence 来自 Intellect, according to Hofstadter, is different from native intelligence, a quality we reluctantly admire.，原文只说两者不同、并指出社会勉强欣赏的是 intelligence，并未说作者认为 intellect 次于 intelligence。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"It evolves from common sense 与 Practicality, common sense, and native intelligence have been considered more noble qualities than anything you could learn from a book. 不符——原文把 common sense 与 intellect 并列对照而非演化关系。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"四个选项中只有 It is to be pursued 给 intellect 一个明确的正面价值定位，与作者全文呼吁智识的态度一致。","pairs":[{"orig":"Encouraging kids to reject the life of the mind leaves them vulnerable to exploitation and control.","opt":"It is to be pursued"},{"orig":"intellect is mistrusted","opt":"It is to be pursued"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"It underlies power 把 Intellect is resented as a form of power or privilege 中 \"被反感成权力的象征\" 反转为 \"它是权力的根基\"，把作者引用的反智借口当成作者本人立场。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-b","kind":"translation","title":"Section II Part C 英译汉","directions":"Directions: Read the following text carefully and then translate the underlined segments into Chinese. Write your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. ( 10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-b-1","text":"The relation of language and mind has interested philosophers for many centuries. (41) The Greeks assumed that the structure of language had some connection with the process of thought, which took root in Europe long before people realized how diverse languages could be."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-2","text":"Only recently did linguists begin the serious study of languages that were very different from their own. Two anthropologist-linguists, Franz Boas and Edward Sapir, were pioneers in describing many native languages of North and South America during the first half of the twentieth century. (42) We are obliged to them because some of these languages have since vanished, as the peoples who spoke them died out or became assimilated and lost their native languages. Other linguists in the earlier part of this century, however, who were less eager to deal with bizarre data from \"exotic\" language, were not always so grateful. (43) The newly described languages were often so strikingly different from the well studied languages of Europe and Southeast Asia that some scholars even accused Boas and Sapir of fabricating their data. Native American languages are indeed different, so much so in fact that Navajo could be used by the US military as a code during World War II to send secret messages."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-3","text":"Sapir's pupil, Benjamin Lee Whorf, continued the study of American Indian languages. (44) Being interested in the relationship of language and thought, Whorf developed the idea that the structure of language determines the structure of habitual thought in a society. He reasoned that because it is easier to formulate certain concepts and not others in a given language, the speakers of that language think along one track and not along another. (45) Whorf came to believe in a sort of linguistic determinism which, in its strongest form, states that language imprisons the mind, and that the grammatical patterns in a language can produce far-reaching consequences for the culture of a society. Later, this idea became known as the Sapir-Whorf hypothesis, but this term is somewhat inappropriate. Although both Sapir and Whorf emphasized the diversity of languages, Sapir himself never explicitly supported the notion of linguistic determinism."}]},"sentences":[{"n":41,"en":"The Greeks assumed that the structure of language had some connection with the process of thought, which took root in Europe long before people realized how diverse languages could be.","refZh":"希腊人认为，语言的结构与思维的过程之间存在某种联系；这一看法早在人们意识到各种语言之间的差异有多大之前，就已在欧洲扎下根。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"The Greeks assumed that","lit":"希腊人认为","role":"（主干主谓 + that 宾语从句引导词）","note":""},{"en":"the structure of language had some connection with the process of thought,","lit":"语言的结构与思维的过程有某种联系，","role":"（that 宾语从句（采分意群））","note":"难点： 抽象名词具体化 the structure of language / the process of thought 两个抽象名词词组按字面译成「语言的结构」「思维的过程」即可，无需再具体化；some connection 不是「一些联系」，some 在此表「某种」（不定指），译作「某种联系」更贴 some connection 的语义。"},{"en":"which took root in Europe","lit":"这一看法在欧洲扎下根","role":"（which 引导的非限制性定语从句（采分意群））","note":"难点： which 回指整个前句命题 which 不是就近指 the process of thought，而是回指「希腊人关于语言结构与思维过程有联系」这一整个观点（见全文锚定）。take root 是固定搭配「生根、扎根」，比喻义即「逐渐被接受/确立下来」。"},{"en":"long before people realized how diverse languages could be.","lit":"远在人们意识到各种语言会有多么不同之前。","role":"（long before 引导的时间状语从句（采分意群））","note":"难点： long before 与 how diverse … could be 的译法 long before 译作「远在…之前」或「早在…之前」；how diverse languages could be 是感叹式从句，could 不译「能够」而译成虚拟语气下的「会有多么…」，整体意思是「人们意识到各种语言间差异有多大」。"}]},{"n":42,"en":"We are obliged to them because some of these languages have since vanished, as the peoples who spoke them died out or became assimilated and lost their native languages.","refZh":"我们对他们心怀感激，因为其中一些语言此后已经消失了——说这些语言的那些民族或者灭绝，或者被同化、失去了自己的母语。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"We are obliged to them","lit":"我们感激他们","role":"（主干主系表（采分意群））","note":"难点： be obliged to sb. 的熟词僻义 obliged 不译「被迫/有义务」，be obliged to sb. 是固定搭配，表「感激某人、对某人心怀感念」（≈be grateful to）。them 按上文锚定回指 Boas 和 Sapir 两位人类学—语言学家，可译出「我们感激这两位学者/我们要感谢他们」。"},{"en":"because some of these languages have since vanished,","lit":"因为其中一些语言此后已经消失了，","role":"（because 原因状语从句（采分意群））","note":"难点： since 作副词「此后」+ 现在完成时 since 在此不是连词「自从…以来」，而是副词「自那以后、此后」，与 have vanished 现在完成时配合，强调「自 Boas/Sapir 当年描写至今的这段时间里已经消失」。these languages 按上文锚定指美洲土著语。"},{"en":"as the peoples who spoke them died out","lit":"因为说这些语言的民族已灭绝","role":"（as 原因状语从句 + who 定语从句（采分意群））","note":"难点： as 表原因 + peoples 的复数义 + 指代还原 as 在此与上文 because 平行表「因为」（再次给出原因，可译「随着…/由于…」）；peoples 加 s 不是「人们」而是「（多个）民族/族群」；who spoke them 中 them 回指 these languages，译时点出「说这些语言的（那些）民族」。"},{"en":"or became assimilated and lost their native languages.","lit":"或者被同化、失去了自己的母语。","role":"（与 died out 并列的两个谓语（采分意群））","note":"难点： 被动语态汉化 + native language 译法 became assimilated 是「become + 过去分词」的被动结构，汉语转为主动或无主句：「被同化/遭到同化」均可；native language 在此语境译「母语/本族语」最稳，对应 lost their native languages。"}]},{"n":43,"en":"The newly described languages were often so strikingly different from the well studied languages of Europe and Southeast Asia that some scholars even accused Boas and Sapir of fabricating their data.","refZh":"这些新近被描写的语言常常与欧洲和东南亚那些已被充分研究的语言差异极其显著，以至于一些学者甚至指责博厄斯和萨丕尔捏造了他们的数据。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"The newly described languages were often so strikingly different from the well studied languages of Europe and Southeast Asia","lit":"这些新近被描写的语言常常与欧洲和东南亚那些已被充分研究的语言差异极其显著，","role":"（主干主系表 + so…that 前半（采分意群））","note":"难点： newly described / well studied 的过去分词作前置定语 newly described 不能译成「新描述的」（生硬），按全文锚定指 Boas/Sapir 当年新近记录下来的美洲土著语，译「新近被描写的/新近记录下来的」；well studied 译「已被充分研究的/研究透彻的」。strikingly different from… 是固定结构「与…显著不同」，strikingly 是程度副词，不能漏译。"},{"en":"that some scholars even accused Boas and Sapir","lit":"以至于一些学者甚至指责 Boas 和 Sapir","role":"（so…that 结果状语从句主干（采分意群））","note":"难点： so…that 结果状语 + even 的语气 so…that 在此是「如此…以至于…」的结果连接，译成「以至于/竟然」即可，不必逐字直译「如此…那么…」；even 的语气不能漏，译「甚至」以体现学者的反应之强烈。"},{"en":"of fabricating their data.","lit":"捏造了他们的数据。","role":"（accuse sb. of doing 的搭配补足语（采分意群））","note":"难点： accuse sb. of doing 固定搭配 + their 指代 accuse sb. of doing sth. 整体译「指控/指责某人做某事」；fabricating 是「捏造、伪造」的贬义动词，不能轻译成「编造」；their data 中 their 回指 Boas 和 Sapir，译时可点明「他们（即 Boas 和 Sapir）的数据」或直接「他们的资料」。"}]},{"n":44,"en":"Being interested in the relationship of language and thought, Whorf developed the idea that the structure of language determines the structure of habitual thought in a society.","refZh":"由于对语言与思维之间的关系感兴趣，沃尔夫逐渐形成了这样一种观点：在一个社会中，语言的结构决定了习惯性思维的结构。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Being interested in the relationship of language and thought,","lit":"由于对语言与思维的关系感兴趣，","role":"（现在分词短语作原因/伴随状语（采分意群））","note":"难点： Being + p.p. 状语的逻辑义 Being interested in… 是现在分词短语，逻辑主语与主句主语 Whorf 一致；语义上表「原因」（≈Because he was interested in…），译「由于/因为对…感兴趣」最贴切，也可译「出于对…的兴趣」。relationship of language and thought 译「语言与思维的关系」（the relationship of A and B 此处等同 relationship between A and B）。"},{"en":"Whorf developed the idea","lit":"沃尔夫提出了这样一种观点","role":"（主干主谓宾）","note":"难点： developed 与 the idea 的搭配义 developed 在此不译「发展了」而译「提出/逐步形成」，与 the idea「观点/看法」搭配，整体表「逐渐形成并提出某一观点」。后接 that 同位语从句，可在「观点」后用冒号或「即/认为」承接。"},{"en":"that the structure of language determines the structure of habitual thought in a society.","lit":"即一个社会中语言的结构决定其习惯性思维的结构。","role":"（the idea 的 that 同位语从句（采分意群））","note":"难点： 同位语 that 从句的识别 + 抽象名词的统一译法 that 在此不是定语从句关系词（that 在从句中不充当成分缺位），而是同位语从句引导词，对前面的 the idea 作内容说明，译时在「观点」后加「即/认为/——」承接。habitual thought 全文统一译「习惯性思维」（也可「思维习惯」，但需与 Q45 保持一致）；in a society 译「在一个社会中/在某个社会里」，是范围状语，不可漏。"}]},{"n":45,"en":"Whorf came to believe in a sort of linguistic determinism which, in its strongest form, states that language imprisons the mind, and that the grammatical patterns in a language can produce far-reaching consequences for the culture of a society.","refZh":"沃尔夫逐渐信奉一种语言决定论。该学说在其最极端的形式下主张：语言禁锢思维；而且一种语言中的语法模式会对一个社会的文化产生深远的影响。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Whorf came to believe in a sort of linguistic determinism","lit":"沃尔夫逐渐相信一种语言决定论","role":"（主干主谓宾（采分意群））","note":"难点： came to do 与 believe in 的搭配 came to believe 是「come to do」结构，表「逐渐开始（相信/认识到）」，强调认识过程，不译「来相信」；believe in 译「信奉/相信（某种学说）」；a sort of 译「一种」即可，不必译「某种类型的」；linguistic determinism 按全文统一译「语言决定论」。"},{"en":"which, in its strongest form, states that","lit":"这种学说，以其最强的形式，主张","role":"（which 引导的非限制性定语从句主干 + 插入语（采分意群））","note":"难点： which 回指 + 插入语处理 + states 取义 which 回指 a sort of linguistic determinism「这种语言决定论」；in its strongest form 是插入语，译「在其最极端的/最强的形式下」或「就其最极端的形式而言」；states 在此不是「陈述」而是「主张/认为/宣称」，与学说搭配。"},{"en":"language imprisons the mind,","lit":"语言禁锢思维，","role":"（states 的第一个 that 宾语从句（采分意群））","note":"难点： imprisons 的比喻义 imprison 字面「监禁/关进监狱」，此处是比喻义，与抽象主语 language 和宾语 the mind 搭配，译「禁锢/束缚」最贴切，呼应作者「imprisons」一词强烈的色彩；mind 译「思维/心灵」均可，此处「思维」与上文 habitual thought 主题一致更佳。"},{"en":"and that the grammatical patterns in a language can produce far-reaching consequences for the culture of a society.","lit":"并且一种语言中的语法模式会对一个社会的文化产生深远的影响。","role":"（states 的第二个 that 宾语从句（与前一 that 并列，采分意群））","note":"难点： 两个 that 并列 + far-reaching consequences 的固定译法 and that… 是与前面 that language imprisons the mind 并列的第二个宾语从句，两 that 都受 states 支配，译时要把两 that 从句作为「主张的两条内容」并列译出，可用「并且/而且」连接；far-reaching consequences for… 是固定搭配，译「对…产生深远的影响/深远的后果」，consequences 在此中性偏负或中性，译「影响/后果」均可。grammatical patterns 译「语法模式/语法结构」。"}]}]},{"id":"section3","kind":"writing","title":"Section III 写作","directions":"46. Directions: Study the following drawing carefully and write an essay in which you should 1. describe the drawing， 2. interpret its meaning, and 3. support your view with examples. You should write about 200 words neatly on ANSWER SHEET 2 (20 points)","prompt":"46. Directions: Study the following drawing carefully and write an essay in which you should 1. describe the drawing， 2. interpret its meaning, and 3. support your view with examples. You should write about 200 words neatly on ANSWER SHEET 2 (20 points)","points":20,"image":{"src":"assets/writing/2004-section3.jpg","alt":"这是一幅黑白漫画，标题是“终点又是新起点”","width":"832","height":"967","local":"assets/writing/2004-section3.jpg"},"model":{"essay":"As is vividly depicted in the cartoon, a boy in a T-shirt printed with the word \"RUN\" is crossing a finish line. Behind him stands an arrow marked \"finish\", while another arrow just ahead of him points into the distance, labeled \"start\". The title, \"The finish line is also a new starting point\", captures the scene at a glance. Simple as the drawing is, it conveys a thought-provoking message about how we should treat success and achievement. The boy has clearly reached a goal, yet the picture reminds us that every ending is merely the beginning of another journey. In other words, no accomplishment should be regarded as a final destination; rather, it ought to serve as a fresh springboard from which we set off toward higher aims. History offers abundant evidence for this view. Many outstanding athletes, after winning an Olympic gold medal, immediately begin preparing for the next competition instead of resting on their laurels. Likewise, a student who is admitted to a top university soon faces new courses and tougher challenges rather than the end of study. Therefore, we should never be content with what we have gained. Only by treating each finish line as a new start can we keep moving forward and realize our full potential.","translation":"正如漫画生动描绘的，一个穿着印有“RUN”字样T恤的男孩正跨过终点线。他身后立着一个标着“终点”的箭头，而就在他前方，另一个箭头指向远方，写着“起点”。标题“终点又是新起点”一眼道出了画面。\n画面虽简单，却传递出一个发人深省的信息，关乎我们该如何看待成功与成就。男孩显然已抵达一个目标，但画面提醒我们：每一个结束不过是另一段旅程的开始。换言之，任何成就都不应被视为最终归宿，而应成为一块新的跳板，让我们由此奔向更高的目标。\n历史为这一观点提供了大量佐证。许多杰出的运动员在赢得奥运金牌之后，会立刻投入下一场比赛的备战，而不是躺在功劳簿上。同样，一名考入顶尖大学的学生，随之而来的是新课程与更艰巨的挑战，而非学业的终点。因此，我们绝不该满足于已有的收获。唯有把每一条终点线都当作新的起点，我们才能不断前行，实现自身全部的潜能。","breakdown":[{"tag":"【第 1 段】","core":"描图段落实白描","text":"【第 1 段】 描图段落实白描 。开篇 As is vividly depicted... 引入，逐一写男孩跨线、T恤 RUN 字样、finish 与 start 两个反向箭头，纯客观描述、不掺评论，落实了 describe the drawing。"},{"tag":"【第 2 段】","core":"主题句立寓意","text":"【第 2 段】 主题句立寓意 。Simple as the drawing is, it conveys... 一句主题句把“终点即新起点”亮出，再用 In other words 递进解释为什么，落实了 interpret its meaning。"},{"tag":"【第 3 段】","core":"两例支撑并收束","text":"【第 3 段】 两例支撑并收束 。用奥运冠军夺金后备战下一场、学生升入名校两个例子支撑观点，末句 Only by... 收尾呼应寓意，落实了 support your view with examples。"}],"wordCount":211}}],"questionCount":40,"objectiveCount":40,"answerTable":{"ans-section1":"完形填空（四选一） Section I （1–20 题） 1 C centering · 2 D because · 3 A interaction · 4 D response · 5 A or · 6 B ignoring · 7 C for · 8 D subject · 9 A affect · 10 B lead · 11 A in general · 12 C turn · 13 D experienced · 14 B consequently · 15 A than · 16 B structure · 17 B identifiable · 18 D availability · 19 A incidence · 20 C although \n（逐题解析见 完形填空（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-1":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (1) （21–25 题） 21 C · 22 A · 23 D · 24 B · 25 C \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-2":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (2) （26–30 题） 26 A · 27 D · 28 C · 29 B · 30 D \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-3":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (3) （31–35 题） 31 D · 32 A · 33 B · 34 A · 35 C \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-4":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (4) （36–40 题） 36 C · 37 A · 38 D · 39 B · 40 C \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-b":"英译汉（划线句子翻译） Section II Part B \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 英译汉（划线句子翻译）解析页","ans-section3":"写作 Section III \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 写作解析页"},"coverage":{"objective":40,"explained":40,"missingSections":[]}};
